{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## HANDOFF to the Jira Server/DC session (epic e369)\n\nReparented here because this is a DC/reconciler-seam decision, not standalone. Summary of the\ngap you now own:\n\n**What is not implemented in production:** the `(inbound, probe)` dispatch chain — rebar's\nmechanism to distinguish a **deleted** Jira issue from one that merely **aged out of the fetch\nwindow** — has NO live producer. `differ._compute_mutations_emit_absent_partner_probes` only\nemits when it sees `local_state[key][\"jira_key\"]`, but its sole production caller\n(`run_differs.py:222`, `compute_mutations(ctx.prev_snapshot, ctx.curr_snapshot, ...)`) passes a\nFETCHED Jira snapshot, whose entries are raw Jira `fields` dicts (`fetcher.py:479`, contract\n`_snapshot_schema.py:96-135`) and carry no `jira_key`. So the loop never fires, and everything\ndownstream is dead in prod: `_run_differs_inbound_probe_dispatch` (run_differs.py),\n`inbound_probe.py` (ProbeResult/ProbeBranch/router), `backend.probe_remote`, the\n`SupportsAbsenceProbe` capability.\n\n**What is not tested (and why the suite is still green):**\n- The DC live cell that would exercise it — `test_a_deleted_dc_issue_never_plans_a_local_teardown`\n  (Row 14, tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py) — is `@_skip`/`@_skip_no_extra`, so\n  it only runs against a real DC with extras; it does not run in normal CI.\n- Even when it runs, its oracle was CORRECTED (ticket b9b8): it NO LONGER asserts an\n  `(inbound, probe)` entry (that citation was wrong/unsatisfiable). It now asserts the real\n  ADR-0028 section-1 observable — deleting the DC issue must NOT plan a local teardown. So the\n  probe path itself is verified NOWHERE.\n- The only fixture that supplies a `jira_key`-bearing `local_state` is the unit test\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_emits_probe.py — a synthetic input the real\n  caller never produces.\n\n**Why it matters for DC:** ADR 0028 relies on the bounded direct GET->404 to PROVE deletion\n(vs aged-out). Today, on DC, that discrimination is exercised only by the outbound differ's\nbounded GET (`outbound_differ.py:692-702`), while the inbound-probe arm is inert.\n\n**The decision you inherit (this ticket's AC #1): wire it or delete it.**\n- WIRE: migrate the caller to pass a `jira_key`-bearing local_state AND — in the SAME change —\n  remove `reconcile_helpers.drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions` (that suppression only\n  exists because the caller passes the legacy prev/curr snapshot pair; migrating makes the\n  suppressed emissions correct again — leaving both silently drops real work). Then un-skip /\n  restore a DC cell that asserts the probe on a confirmed-deleted bound pair.\n- DELETE: remove the dead chain (inbound_probe.py, the dispatch arm, the capability) and accept\n  deletion detection stays solely on the outbound-GET path.\n\nFull analysis and the \"what is NOT the fix\" warning are in this ticket's description. No code\nhas been changed for this ticket."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785868094510098001,"uuid":"aa5f057d-2421-4347-8dda-8b76fca1ec7d"}